# TypeScript/JavaScript Patterns

> This file extends [common/patterns.md](../common/patterns.md) with TypeScript/JavaScript specific content.

## API Response Format

Errors follow RFC 9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`) — no custom
success/error envelope. Success responses are plain DTOs; paginated responses share
one metadata shape. *(Kanōn)* Validate at the boundary with Zod.

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod'

const problemDetailsSchema = z.object({
  type: z.string().url().optional(),
  title: z.string(),
  status: z.number().int(),
  detail: z.string().optional(),
  instance: z.string().optional(),
})
type ProblemDetails = z.infer<typeof problemDetailsSchema>

interface Page<T> {
  items: T[]
  total: number
  page: number
  size: number
}

async function apiFetch<T>(url: string, schema: z.ZodType<T>): Promise<T> {
  const res = await fetch(url)
  if (!res.ok) {
    throw new ApiError(problemDetailsSchema.parse(await res.json()))
  }
  return schema.parse(await res.json())
}
```

## Custom Hooks Pattern

```typescript
export function useDebounce<T>(value: T, delay: number): T {
  const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState<T>(value)

  useEffect(() => {
    const handler = setTimeout(() => setDebouncedValue(value), delay)
    return () => clearTimeout(handler)
  }, [value, delay])

  return debouncedValue
}
```

## Repository Pattern

```typescript
interface Repository<T> {
  findAll(filters?: Filters): Promise<T[]>
  findById(id: string): Promise<T | null>
  create(data: CreateDto): Promise<T>
  update(id: string, data: UpdateDto): Promise<T>
  delete(id: string): Promise<void>
}
```

